### 4. ⚠️ HIGH: A05:2021 – Broken Access Control (CWE-639)
**Severity: HIGH**

#### Issues Found:
- **No authentication layer**: Anyone can access all endpoints
- **No authorization checks**: No role-based access control (RBAC)
- **No audit logging**: No tracking of who accessed what data
- **No session management**: No timeout protection

#### Recommendations:

```javascript
// Implement role-based access control

const roles = {
  admin: ['read:users', 'write:users', 'delete:users'],
  user: ['read:profile'],
  guest: ['read:health'],
};

const authorize = (requiredPermissions) => {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!req.user) {
      return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Authentication required' });
    }

    const userRole = req.user.role;
    const userPermissions = roles[userRole] || [];

    const hasPermission = requiredPermissions.every(perm => 
      userPermissions.includes(perm)
    );

    if (!hasPermission) {
      // Log unauthorized access attempt
      console.warn(`Unauthorized access attempt: user ${req.user.id} (${userRole}) tried to access ${req.path}`);
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient permissions' });
    }

    next();
  };
};

// Usage
app.get('/users', verifyToken, authorize(['read:users']), (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
