371	### 10. **No Error Handling / Information Disclosure (OWASP A01: Broken Access Control)**
372	
373	**Issue:** Generic error responses and potential stack trace exposure.
374	
375	**Risk Level:** MEDIUM
376	- Stack traces can leak sensitive information
377	- Users might see internal implementation details
378	
379	**Recommended Fix:**
380	```javascript
381	// Global error handler
382	app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
383	  logger.error({
384	    message: err.message,
385	    stack: err.stack,
386	    url: req.url,
387	    method: req.method,
388	  });
389	
390	  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
391	    // Don't expose error details in production
392	    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
393	  }
394	
395	  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
396	    error: err.message,
397	    ...(process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' && { stack: err.stack }),
398	  });
399	});
400	
401	// 404 handler
402	app.use((req, res) => {
403	  res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
404	});
405	```
